---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Corporate, Commercial & Compliance" description="Corporate structuring, commercial transactions, incorporation, and regulatory, tax, AML and data-protection compliance under Cameroonian, OHADA and CEMAC law.">
<div>
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(48px,7vw,104px) clamp(20px,5vw,80px) clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
    <a href="/practices/" class="lnk" style="background:none;border:0;padding:0;cursor:pointer;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#007EA7;margin-bottom:26px">← Practices</a>
    <h1 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(36px,5.2vw,68px);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;max-width:22ch">Corporate, Commercial &amp; Compliance</h1>
    <p style="font-size:clamp(17px,1.4vw,20px);line-height:1.7;color:#38484f;max-width:66ch;margin:32px 0 0">We advise companies and organisations on how they are structured, how they contract, and how they meet their regulatory obligations under Cameroonian, OHADA and CEMAC law.</p>
  </section>
  <hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);margin:0" />
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,80px)">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <aside style="grid-column:span 3;min-width:200px;align-self:start;position:sticky;top:110px;padding:clamp(32px,4vw,56px) 0">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7b82;margin-bottom:18px">On this page</div>
        <nav style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;border-left:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16);padding-left:18px">
          <span style="font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#007EA7">Corporate &amp; Commercial</span>
          <a href="#structuring" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Structuring and restructuring</a>
          <a href="#transactions" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Commercial transactions</a>
          <a href="#incorporation" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Incorporation and formation</a>
          <span style="font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#007EA7;margin-top:10px">Compliance &amp; Governance</span>
          <a href="#regulatory" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Regulatory compliance</a>
          <a href="#governance" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Governance frameworks</a>
          <a href="#tax" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Tax compliance</a>
          <a href="#aml" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">AML compliance</a>
          <a href="#data" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Data protection</a>
          <a href="#ngo" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">NGO and organisational policy</a>
          <a href="#faq" style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:#00171F">Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </aside>
      <div style="grid-column:span 8;min-width:280px;padding:clamp(32px,4vw,56px) 0 clamp(48px,6vw,88px)">

        <section id="structuring" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:0 0 44px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Corporate structuring and restructuring</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">We advise on how a business should be organised: the choice of vehicle, the allocation of shares and control, group structures and holding arrangements, and the changes that follow growth, investment or a change of ownership.</p><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Restructuring work includes capital increases and reductions, conversions between company forms, share transfers, mergers and reorganisations within a group, and the amendments to articles and registrations each step requires.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="transactions" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Commercial transactions</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Drafting, review and negotiation of the agreements a business runs on: supply, services and distribution contracts, commercial agency, licensing, shareholder and joint-venture agreements, and terms of business.</p><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">We draft to be enforced. Contracts are prepared in English, French or both, with governing-law and dispute-resolution provisions chosen for where the counterparty and its assets actually are.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="incorporation" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Company incorporation and business formation</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">We take businesses from first decision to registration under the OHADA Uniform Act on Commercial Companies: choice of vehicle, articles of association, capital deposit, notarial steps, registration at the RCCM and the tax and social-security registrations that follow.</p><dl style="margin:18px 0 0;display:grid;gap:14px;max-width:68ch"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(90px,120px) 1fr;gap:20px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1);padding-top:14px"><dt style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600">SA</dt><dd style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61">Public company. Board or sole-administrator governance, statutory auditor, higher minimum capital. Suited to regulated businesses and ventures with institutional shareholders.</dd></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(90px,120px) 1fr;gap:20px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1);padding-top:14px"><dt style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600">SARL</dt><dd style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61">The default operating company. Manager-run, flexible capital, share transfers subject to statutory and contractual consent.</dd></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(90px,120px) 1fr;gap:20px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1);padding-top:14px"><dt style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600">SAS</dt><dd style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61">Contractual freedom in the articles: tailored share classes, veto rights and transfer mechanics.</dd></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(90px,120px) 1fr;gap:20px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1);padding-top:14px"><dt style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600">GIE</dt><dd style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61">Economic interest group for pooled activity between existing businesses.</dd></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(90px,120px) 1fr;gap:20px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.1);padding-top:14px"><dt style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600">Branch</dt><dd style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4a5a61">Registration of a foreign company’s branch, with its statutory duration limits and conversion requirements.</dd></div></dl>
        </section>

        <section id="regulatory" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Regulatory compliance advisory</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Advice on the licences, authorisations and ongoing obligations that apply to a business in its sector, and on how to organise compliance so that it can be demonstrated to a regulator. We work with clients in banking and finance, payments, telecommunications, logistics, and oil and gas.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="governance" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Corporate governance frameworks</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Board and management structures, delegations of authority, internal rules, and the policies that allow a company to show how decisions are made and recorded. We review existing frameworks against the Uniform Act and the company’s own articles, and draft what is missing.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="tax" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Tax compliance</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Legal support on corporate tax obligations under the General Tax Code: registration, the tax consequences of structuring and transfers, withholding on payments, and responses to enquiries from the tax administration. We work alongside clients’ accountants and tax advisers.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="aml" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">AML compliance</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Advice on anti-money-laundering and counter-terrorist-financing obligations under the CEMAC framework: customer due diligence, record-keeping, suspicious-transaction reporting, and the internal policies and training that regulated entities are expected to maintain.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="data" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Data protection</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Advice on the collection, use, storage and transfer of personal data under Cameroonian law: privacy notices, consent, data-processing agreements with service providers, cross-border transfers, and internal data-handling policies for employees and customers.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="ngo" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14)">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">NGO and organisational policy review</h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 0px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">For non-governmental organisations, human resources firms and other organisations: review of constitutions, governance documents and internal policies — including conduct, safeguarding, procurement and staff policies — with recommendations and redrafts that strengthen accountability.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="faq" style="scroll-margin-top:110px;padding:44px 0 0;">
          <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,2.4vw,32px);line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 20px">Questions we are asked</h2><div style="max-width:68ch">
            <details style="border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16);padding:18px 0"><summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:16.5px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.5;color:#00171F;list-style:none">Which vehicle should a new business use in Cameroon?</summary><p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#4a5a61">Most new operations are a SARL, for its light governance, or an SAS where shareholders want tailored arrangements in the articles. A branch can suit a foreign company testing the market but is time-limited. The right answer depends on licensing, the shareholders and the planned exit.</p></details>
            <details style="border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16);padding:18px 0"><summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:16.5px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.5;color:#00171F;list-style:none">Can our contracts be governed by English law?</summary><p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#4a5a61">Commercial contracts between sophisticated parties often can be. Company constitutions, employment relationships and interests in Cameroonian land remain subject to local and OHADA law, so we usually split the document suite rather than force one governing law across it.</p></details>
            <details style="border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16);padding:18px 0"><summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:16.5px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.5;color:#00171F;list-style:none">How long does incorporation take?</summary><p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#4a5a61"><span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:14px;color:#6b7b82">[Indicative timetable to be confirmed by the firm.]</span> Timing depends on notarial steps, the capital deposit, the registry’s turnaround and whether a sector licence is needed before trading.</p></details>
            <details style="border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16);padding:18px 0"><summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:16.5px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.5;color:#00171F;list-style:none">Do you work in English and French?</summary><p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#4a5a61">Yes. Advice, correspondence and negotiation follow the client’s language; filings follow the language of the authority. We also translate legal documents between English and French.</p></details>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7b82;margin:28px 0 0;max-width:68ch">General information about the firm’s practice, not legal advice. No lawyer-client relationship arises from reading this page.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
